{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/144244-alchymists-of-most-noble-good","id":144244,"title":"Alchymists of Most Noble Good","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-21T00:59:29-07:00","id":144244,"title":"Alchymists of Most Noble Good","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Evil into good, that is my vow.</span></i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Isn\u2019t it a wonderful thing that the Devil exists? Now if you\u2019re confused by that statement you\u2019re in the good company. Most Changelings would say that it is utterly unfair that both the Gentry and the Infernal are allowed to exist, one would be enough for any world. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The alcheymists see it differently. The chemical saints believe that the Inferno is cosmologically significant in a way that the Gentry are not, an absolute origin point and frame of reference for evil. More importantly, demons are an absolute origin point that can be punched in the face. The alchemyists believe that demons are the weak point in evil, defeat the demons and good will triumph over the world. Naturally they dedicate themselves to this task. Killing a demon is good, but the Entitlement\u2019s true mission - the reason they are named Alchymists - is to transform demons into something good; they do this using a power only the fae have, the power of Pledges. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Despite what the name would imply, the chemical saints\u2019 closest analogue would be a monastic military order. The Entitlement is devoutly Abrahamic, filled with traditions, behavioural vows, and codes of conducts. The abrahamic faith is a divided one and these divisions are reflected upon the Noble Alchymists, Chemical Saints of different denominations often like each other as people, but are usually unable to live together due to conflicting vows and codes. The Entitelment\u2019s typical response is to just ignore the whole thing and act as though their chapter is the entirety of the Entitlement. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Member Titles: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Noble Alchymist, Noble Alchemist, Chemical Saint. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Picture</span></b><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> A gnome wearing an open brown labcoat, A long parchment is stitched to one breast of the coat, hanging loose. He wields a rangun-style chemical spray weapon and a grappling hook gun. Both are covered in alchemical and catholic decorations. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Requirements: </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wyrd 5, Clarity 6+, Willpower 6, Academics 3, one of Brawl, Firearms or Weapons at three. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Joining:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Membership of the Chemical Saints is a three step process: First the initiate must travel to one of the monasteries (there\u2019s only a few in the world, but they\u2019re in the Hedge so you can reach them by walking from just about anywhere) and convince the master that you\u2019re worthy of service. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The second stage is monastic life. The initiate must live and train as one of the Chemical Saints, proving that they can live up to the ideals and vows expected of all Alchymists. This typically lasts for a month to a year. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The final stage is your first quest. The initiate must find and deal with a demon, an initiate may go alone or in a group of initiates though the Wyrd typically provides a greater challenge for a group and if it doesn\u2019t the initiates may be sent out again to find a worthier challenge. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mein:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> A Chemical Saint\u2019s Mein becomes bolder, dashing, inspiring. They are radiant, with not a hair out of place. No scar or dirt from their battles remains for long.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Background:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> You might be surprised to learn that more Chemical Saints hail from Autumn than Summer. The Iron Spear are better fighters, that much is undeniable, but they are motivated by Wrath, righteous anger against their former captors. The Autumn Court seek a new beginning in the faerie world, to use what the Gentry gave them and create a life for themselves. In their exploration they may learn occult lore about the Inferno and a way to find meaning in the faerie abilities they never asked for. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Further afield you can find alchymists hailing from both the Dawn and Sun courts. The hope enshrined by Dawn fits well with the ideal of vanquishing evil itself. As for the White Hill, the elders of the Sun Court might gripe that youngsters who believe you can vanquish evil are missing the point, but the Durandal Courts have been filed with gripping elders and stubborn youngsters since the beginning. Travel further east and you\u2019ll find that both the Stupa and the Sword fit well with the lifestyle of the Entitlement. However the abrahamic faiths have not dominated the Directional Courts\u2019 heartlands as they have elsewhere and so fewer members hail from those courts than you might expect. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Whatever court they came from, the chemical saints tend to be disciplined people before they joined. Many also felt a sense of dissatisfaction with the glamour and chaos of faerie society. They didn\u2019t want to hide, they wanted to stand tall, to stand for something. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Organisation</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">: The chemical saints divide themselves into chapters, each centered around a fortress-monastery in the Hedge. Each chapter lives by it\u2019s own code and follows a different branch of the Abrahamic faith, there\u2019s nothing to prevent two Catholic chapters existing but the Entitlement just isn\u2019t that big. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">For most alchemists their monastery is the closest thing they\u2019ll have to a home. They live on the road, tracking down demon after demon. Others live in a freehold, particularly if it\u2019s in a large urban area where there\u2019s plenty of demons to hunt. These Chemical Saints see themselves as protectors of the freehold from infernal threats, many also moonlight as Pledge lawyers. The Entitlement\u2019s skill at pledges is renowned as the fate of any who suffers a curse of vulnerability against them. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Privileges: </span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Laws from Heaven: There are two types of being truly renowned for their still at bargains and contracts. The Fae and the Infernal. To weave contracts and trickery on helpless mortals, any fae is capable of that. To do the same to a demon, that takes the best of faerie kind. The Chemical Saints train themselves to be that best, and all have three dots in the Pledgesmith merit. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Reliquary of Arms: Pledgebinding a demon is the ideal but not always practical, so the Chemical Saints travel armed. When a Chemical Saint performs a notable act of valor, such as their initiation rite, they are given the right to wield one of the Entitlement\u2019s relics. A weapon, normally blinged to the nines with religious and alchemical iconography, that has been passed down the Entitlement for generations since some famous battle. The character gains a two dot Hedgespun Weapon or Token weapon which, in addition to it\u2019s normal damage type, deals holy damage. Players may spend merit dots to buy a better or additional weapons, either earning a more venerated relic through another act of valor or creating one out of whichever non-relic they were using at the time - you have to decorate new relics yourself.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Unbreakable Faith: Clarity can be lost through immoral fae-like behaviour on the Changeling\u2019s part, but also from damage to a changeling\u2019s mind. The sort of damage a demon might inflict. The Chemical Saints are trained to protect themselves, by praying for one hour in an Abrahamic temple, (including the ones in the Entitlement\u2019s Hollows) the changeling automatically succeeds on their next roll to prevent Clarity loss, unless the Breaking Point was caused by their own immorality. In that case they suffer a one die penalty to the roll. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Lead into Gold: The final Privilage of the Alchymists is to turn lead into gold, an evil demon into something good. They are taught a Pledge to bind demons, a pledge to perform no act unless it is good. The fact demons seem to be able to honour this pledge (no matter how much they hate it) is taken as proof by the Chemical Saints that demons truly are an absolute cosmological axis of morality. Normally the pledge is a one sided one with the Alchymist just witnessing the demons careless words before the Wyrd; if it is one sided then it will not count towards the Changeling\u2019s maximum Pledges or cost extra duration or sanction. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">This is the typical form of the Pledge: </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Task: Greater Forbiddance (-3): Any act which is evil. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Boon: Greater Blessing (-3): A three dot merit to provide Essence, since otherwise the demon will starve from a lack of evil long before redeeming itself. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sanction: Death (+3) </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Duration: Lifetime (-3)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Rumours:</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">So where does a group who spend all their time hunting demons get the cash to build a whole set of fortresses in the Hedge? And those military grade weapons underneath all the decorations, stealing isn\u2019t their style is it? They\u2019ve got support, someone or something is funding the Alchemists. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You\u2019ve read the stories right, and for us stories are practically rulebooks. You know that the Lord of Sunday doesn\u2019t like faeries. And now we\u2019ve got this group going around with all that holier than you and praying to you-know-who before fighting demons. Trust me, no matter how noble they seem you do not want to get too close</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-16-2014, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T01:07:40-07:00","id":144284,"title":"","content":"On another thread I described these guys as Demon hunting faerie space marine lawyers.<br /> <br /> Much like 40ks Space Marines, these guys combine the attitude of a military monastic order with very modern weapons, or their hedge spun equivalents. Visually I'd say they're a mixture of heroes like the Rocketeer or Dan Dare, mixed with the Space Marines tendency to cover everything with decorations (and hand down weapons as relics), and a touch of the <a href=\"http://www.imfdb.org/wiki/Romeo_%2B_Juliet#Tybalt.27s_.27Rapier_9mm_Series_R.27\" target=\"_blank\">Tyblalt from Baz Luhrmann's version of Romeo and Juliet. </a><br /> <br /> <br /> The first Rumour is an allusion to the Lucifgue's reconciliation having a similar idea in Dream Catchers.<br /> <br /> The idea of pledgebinding demons like this obviously came from Planescape: Torment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-21-2014, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T01:28:21-07:00","id":144296,"title":"","content":"Interesting. They see to have more benefits then normal both going in opposite directions though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T02:21:31-07:00","id":144314,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you mean by opposite directions; but they're an Eldrich Entitlement (check the Wyrd Requirements) so they are supposed to get more benefits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T09:21:01-07:00","id":144527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/144244-alchymists-of-most-noble-good?p=144314#post144314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you mean by opposite directions; but they're an Eldrich Entitlement (check the Wyrd Requirements) so they are supposed to get more benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen many get four. It just feels like it does too many things. Two pledge powers. One mental dominion ability. One combat ability. It feels like too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T11:47:13-07:00","id":144660,"title":"","content":"Nah, they all make thematic sense. That's the only thing that really matters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T12:25:18-07:00","id":144706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/144244-alchymists-of-most-noble-good?p=144660#post144660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, they all make thematic sense. That's the only thing that really matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking thought them though they only have three powers none of the examples have any less or more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T12:37:28-07:00","id":144720,"title":"","content":"If it makes you feel better treat the first two as one power (five dots of Merits, same as The Charmed Circle's first power)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:43:54-07:00","id":144871,"title":"","content":"problem with the pledge. It says <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">any act which is <u>not</u> evil is forbidden by the pledge.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T19:41:27-07:00","id":145157,"title":"","content":"I don't want to ruin anyone's fun, but I find this odd because thematically Changeling is (somewhat) amoral. Changelings have Clarity instead of Morality, get back willpower by exercising virtues or vices, etc. The base WoD, Vampire, Demon, and Hunter seem like better fits for this group than the Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T19:44:20-07:00","id":145159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quynce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/144244-alchymists-of-most-noble-good?p=145157#post145157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to ruin anyone's fun, but I find this odd because thematically Changeling is (somewhat) amoral. Changelings have Clarity instead of Morality, get back willpower by exercising virtues or vices, etc. The base WoD, Vampire, Demon, and Hunter seem like better fits for this group than the Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>It really doesn't help that inferno demons are rare as hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T00:00:58-07:00","id":145353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bwgustaf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/144244-alchymists-of-most-noble-good?p=144871#post144871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">problem with the pledge. It says <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">any act which is <u>not</u> evil is forbidden by the pledge.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quynce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/144244-alchymists-of-most-noble-good?p=145157#post145157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to ruin anyone's fun, but I find this odd because thematically Changeling is (somewhat) amoral. Changelings have Clarity instead of Morality, get back willpower by exercising virtues or vices, etc. The base WoD, Vampire, Demon, and Hunter seem like better fits for this group than the Lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically Changeling is somewhat amoral, but the Lost know this and some of them intentionally try not to be. As I mentioned in post #2, the first rumour is about an allience with a hunter group doing the same thing. But maybe it's just a rumour?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-16-2014, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T01:26:03-07:00","id":145400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/144244-alchymists-of-most-noble-good?p=145159#post145159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It really doesn't help that inferno demons are rare as hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal demons are actually very scaleable depending on how much of a hellhole you construct your games. Remember, every level 5 Morality (or if your using GMC, Integrity) break can potentially spit out a Whisperer and once they get powerful enough to have a name, or become a Dominion, they can worm themselves into damn near anywhere. Astral Realm has them, the Shadow has them by the boatload, and Twilight most certainly has them.<br /> <br /> The creature is adaptable and the habitat is most certainly plentiful. If you don't see them around, that's to be expected. After all it's in their nature to lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T07:45:51-07:00","id":145657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/144244-alchymists-of-most-noble-good?p=145400#post145400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Infernal demons are actually very scaleable depending on how much of a hellhole you construct your games. Remember, every level 5 Morality (or if your using GMC, Integrity) break can potentially spit out a Whisperer and once they get powerful enough to have a name, or become a Dominion, they can worm themselves into damn near anywhere. Astral Realm has them, the Shadow has them by the boatload, and Twilight most certainly has them.<br /> <br /> The creature is adaptable and the habitat is most certainly plentiful. If you don't see them around, that's to be expected. After all it's in their nature to lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that this won't come up except in very niche games it's an OOC issue more than an IC one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T08:04:11-07:00","id":145668,"title":"","content":"That's not a problem. Just discuss how many demons you plan to include before before anyone joins the Entitlement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T12:43:15-07:00","id":145930,"title":"","content":"Also, do I detect a hint of someone trying to worm the Divine Fire into a Changeling game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T13:05:53-07:00","id":145948,"title":"","content":"The Alchemical theme. The presence of the Abrahamic God that has at times been hypothesised to be a certain Principle. Transformation from a monster into something better.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's actually all a massive coincidence. Honest.<br /> <br /> I can't actually remember exactly how the various parts in this mix came together, but the Divine Fire never even came up for consideration. In my WoD the Empyerian mentioned in Inferno is entirely seperate from the Divine Fire; I really like the classics, Zeus, Odin, Isis, etc and need somewhere to put them. So if you ever see me talking about Inferno and god(s) in the same post I probably mean the Empyrean and not the Fire. <br /> <br /> Plus, I never give the Fire to anyone but Promethians, mad scientists and alchemists (actual alchemists, which these guys aren't) to preserve it's niche as the most mysterious and perhaps awesome thing in the WoD. <br /> <br /> But if the Principle is the Abrahamic God in your WoD, go right ahead. The Alchemical metaphors just make it work even better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T08:28:39-07:00","id":146781,"title":"","content":"not my thing. i like to keep my changeling games running on a phantasmagorical, fairytale vibe. i like to keep grammaton clerics to a minimum.<br /> <br /> looks fun if that is your thing, tho!<br /> <br /> good job!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T09:35:03-07:00","id":146853,"title":"","content":"What's more faerie tale than knights in shining armour <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but seriously, I can respect that viewpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T14:51:07-07:00","id":147178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/144244-alchymists-of-most-noble-good?p=145948#post145948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Alchemical theme. The presence of the Abrahamic God that has at times been hypothesised to be a certain Principle. Transformation from a monster into something better.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's actually all a massive coincidence. Honest.<br /> <br /> I can't actually remember exactly how the various parts in this mix came together, but the Divine Fire never even came up for consideration. In my WoD the Empyerian mentioned in Inferno is entirely seperate from the Divine Fire; I really like the classics, Zeus, Odin, Isis, etc and need somewhere to put them. So if you ever see me talking about Inferno and god(s) in the same post I probably mean the Empyrean and not the Fire.<br /> <br /> Plus, I never give the Fire to anyone but Promethians, mad scientists and alchemists (actual alchemists, which these guys aren't) to preserve it's niche as the most mysterious and perhaps awesome thing in the WoD.<br /> <br /> But if the Principle is the Abrahamic God in your WoD, go right ahead. The Alchemical metaphors just make it work even better.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Principle, depending on my mood, is either the power source of the God-Machine, An Exarch who decided tyranny wasn't for him, An avatar of the Final Watchtower (ripping off Stephen King's The Dark Tower) of which holds everything together, an agent of the Abrahamic god that functions much akin to the GM, or something more weird.<br /> <br /> However, the themes that you are grabbing at along with the mood does sync well with PtC thus my reason for asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}